        <body>
            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="0599" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.032/4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-09-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 19, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 948.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to the
                    Department the text in English and Spanish of the message read by President de
                    la Barra on the occasion of the opening of the first period of the Mexican
                    Congress, on the 16th instant, for the fiscal year 1911–12. The attention of the
                    Department is especially called to that portion of the message which relates to
                    the attitude of the Mexican Government concerning the payment of claims growing
                    out of the recent revolution.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d775-a1.xml" xpointer="d775-a1"/>
